gps-station (0.2.0) stable; urgency=medium

  * First packaged release.
  * gps-station: puts the GPS refclock in
    /etc/ntpsec/conf.d/gps-station.conf, included once from ntp.conf, with
    "tos minsane 1" so the GPS alone can set the clock; calibrates its
    NMEA delay against network time once; warns when gpsd lacks -n; sets
    the grid square on sbitx and zbitxre. Removing the package takes the
    ntpsec changes out again.
  * gps-station-desktop: tray icon showing the fix, the time source and
    whether ticked programs match, with a window that keeps the grid square
    of running ham programs (radio, WSJT-X, JTDX, JS8Call, fldigi, QSSTV),
    shows a sky map of the satellites and what the clock follows.
  * gps-station-lo-multicast.service: turn on multicast for the loopback
    interface at boot, so WSJT-X can share its UDP stream on lo.
  * Man pages for gps-station(8) and gps-station-desktop(1).

 -- Jeffrey Honig <jch@honig.net>  Sun, 25 Oct 2026 14:00:00 -0400
